   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The fundamental distinction between worden and geworden",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **werden** has two forms of past participle depending on its syntactic function: **worden** acts as the auxiliary of the process passive together with another participle (**Der Gesetzesentwurf ist verabschiedet worden**), while **geworden** acts as the participle of the full or copulative verb werden with the sense of becoming (**Der Jurist ist Richter geworden** / **Das Verfahren ist kompliziert geworden**)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Practical mnemonic criterion",
     "texto": [
      "If the sentence has another previous Partizip II that expresses the action suffered by the subject (**unterschrieben, geliefert, repariert**), the final form is compulsorily **worden**. If there is only a noun or an attributive/predicative adjective, the form is **geworden**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Structure",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Syntactic function",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
